  "summary_en": "Mauritius' 2018 national AI strategy by a government working group. It proposes a Mauritius AI Council, priority AI projects in manufacturing, health, fintech, agriculture, energy and ocean economy, incentives, skills building, data protection amendments and human override of AI decisions. Robotics and drones appear only incidentally.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Establish a Mauritius Artificial Intelligence Council (MAIC) of about 10 members to oversee implementation",
   "Private-sector-driven projects supported by matching grants, tax credits and training grants",
   "Priority sectors: manufacturing, healthcare, fintech, agriculture, energy, ocean economy and smart infrastructure",
   "Amend data protection legislation via a special working group; consider open data policy and a government data centre",
   "Legal framework should ensure humans can override AI decisions and keep control"
